package Libraries.Game.Physics

use Libraries.Game.Layer3D
use Libraries.Interface.Item3D
use Libraries.Game.Physics.Joints.JointEdge3D

/*
A PhysicsBehavior3D takes part in a layer's physics
without being an item itself. Joints, which connect two items, are physics
behaviors. So is a vehicle, which pushes on its body every physics step to
model its wheels and suspension.

A behavior is added to a Layer3D in the same way as an item, using Add, and
taken out using Remove. While it is in a layer, the layer calls its actions at
set points in the game loop:

1. AddedToLayer, once, when the behavior is added.
2. UpdatePhysics, once for every physics step. Physics runs in fixed steps,
   normally 1/60 of a second each, so this may run zero, one, or several
   times in a single frame. It is called after the items have moved for that
   step, so it sees where they are now.
3. UpdateAfterPhysics, once per frame, after the items have been placed where
   they will be drawn. This is the place to move anything that should follow
   the physics, such as a vehicle's wheel models.
4. RemovedFromLayer, once, when the behavior is removed.

While the layer is calling UpdatePhysics or UpdateAfterPhysics, a behavior
should not add or remove behaviors or items in that layer. Make those
changes from the game's Update action instead.

All of these actions do nothing by default, so a new behavior only needs to
provide the ones it uses.

A behavior can also report which items it uses, with GetItemsSize and
GetItem.

Attribute: Example

        class Wind is PhysicsBehavior3D
        Item3D target = undefined
        Vector3 force

        action SetTarget(Item3D item)
            target = item
        end

        action SetForce(number x, number y, number z)
            force:Set(x, y, z)
        end

        action UpdatePhysics(number timeStep)
            if target not= undefined
                Vector3 impulse
                impulse:Set(force)
                impulse:Scale(timeStep)
                target:ApplyLinearImpulseToCenter(impulse)
            end
        end

        action GetItemsSize returns integer
            if target = undefined
                return 0
            end
            return 1
        end

        action GetItem(integer index) returns Item3D
            if index = 0
                return target
            end
            return undefined
        end
    end

    // Then, in a game:
    //     Wind wind
    //     wind:SetTarget(box)
    //     wind:SetForce(5, 0, 0)
    //     layer:Add(box)
    //     layer:Add(wind)
*/
class PhysicsBehavior3D
    Layer3D layer = undefined
    
    
    boolean inCollisionGroup = false
    
    /*
    This action returns whether this behavior is a joint, which connects two
    items so that the physics system solves them together. By default it
    returns false. Joint3D returns true.

    Attribute: Returns true if this behavior is a joint, and false otherwise.
    */
    action IsJoint returns boolean
        return false
    end
    
    
    /*
    This action returns whether the physics system has already placed this
    behavior in a group of items to solve together during the current
    physics step. The layer clears this at the start of every step. Most
    users never need to call this action.

    Attribute: Returns true if the behavior is already in a group this step, and false otherwise.
    */
    action InCollisionGroup returns boolean
        return inCollisionGroup
    end

    /*
    This action records whether the physics system has placed this behavior
    in a group of items to solve together during the current physics step.
    Most users never need to call this action.

    Attribute: Parameter flag true if the behavior is now in a group.
    */
    action SetInCollisionGroup(boolean flag)
        me:inCollisionGroup = flag
    end
    
    /*
    This action returns how many edges this behavior uses to connect items.
    An edge links an item to the behavior, so that when the physics system
    gathers items that affect each other, it finds the behavior through the
    item and also includes the item on the other end. Joints use one edge
    for each of their two items. By default a behavior connects nothing, and
    this returns 0.

    Attribute: Returns The number of edges this behavior uses.
    */
    action GetEdgesSize returns integer
        return 0
    end

    /*
    This action returns one of this behavior's edges. Indexes start at 0 and
    go up to one less than GetEdgesSize. By default it returns undefined.

    Attribute: Parameter index The index of the edge.
    Attribute: Returns The edge at that index.
    */
    action GetEdge(integer index) returns JointEdge3D
        return undefined
    end

    /*
    This action returns the item an edge is attached to: the item whose list
    of joints holds the edge. By default it returns undefined.

    Attribute: Parameter index The index of the edge.
    Attribute: Returns The item the edge is attached to.
    */
    action GetEdgeItem(integer index) returns Item3D
        return undefined
    end

    /*
    This action returns the item at the other end of an edge. When the
    physics system reaches this behavior through the edge's item, it also
    includes this one. By default it returns undefined.

    Attribute: Parameter index The index of the edge.
    Attribute: Returns The item at the other end of the edge.
    */
    action GetEdgeOther(integer index) returns Item3D
        return undefined
    end

    /*
    This action attaches each of this behavior's edges to its item, using
    GetEdgesSize, GetEdge, GetEdgeItem, and GetEdgeOther. A Layer3D calls it
    when the behavior is added. Edges whose item is undefined are skipped.
    Most users should never need to call or replace this action.
    */
    action LinkEdges
        integer i = 0
        repeat while i < GetEdgesSize()
            JointEdge3D edge = GetEdge(i)
            Item3D item = GetEdgeItem(i)
            if edge not= undefined and item not= undefined
                edge:SetOther(GetEdgeOther(i))
                edge:SetPrevious(undefined)
                edge:SetNext(item:GetJointList())
                if item:GetJointList() not= undefined
                    item:GetJointList():SetPrevious(edge)
                end
                item:SetJointList(edge)
            end
            i = i + 1
        end
    end

    /*
    This action detaches each of this behavior's edges from its item, and
    wakes the item, since it may now move differently. A Layer3D calls it
    when the behavior is removed. Most users should never need to call or
    replace this action.
    */
    action UnlinkEdges
        integer i = 0
        repeat while i < GetEdgesSize()
            JointEdge3D edge = GetEdge(i)
            Item3D item = GetEdgeItem(i)
            if edge not= undefined and item not= undefined
                item:Simulate(true)

                if edge:GetPrevious() not= undefined
                    edge:GetPrevious():SetNext(edge:GetNext())
                end
                if edge:GetNext() not= undefined
                    edge:GetNext():SetPrevious(edge:GetPrevious())
                end
                if edge = item:GetJointList()
                    item:SetJointList(edge:GetNext())
                end

                edge:SetPrevious(undefined)
                edge:SetNext(undefined)
            end
            i = i + 1
        end
    end

    /*
    This action is called by a Layer3D when this behavior is added to it,
    before any physics steps run. Use it to connect the behavior to the items
    it works with. By default it does nothing.

    Most users never need to call this action directly.

    Attribute: Parameter layer The layer this behavior was added to.
    */
    action AddedToLayer(Layer3D layer)
    end

    /*
    This action is called by a Layer3D when this behavior is removed from it. After this, the
    layer no longer calls the behavior. Use it to undo anything done in
    AddedToLayer. By default it does nothing.

    Most users never need to call this action directly.

    Attribute: Parameter layer The layer this behavior was removed from.
    */
    action RemovedFromLayer(Layer3D layer)
    end

    /*
    This action is called by a Layer3D once for every physics step, after
    the items in the layer have moved for that step. Physics runs in fixed
    steps, so this may be called zero, one, or several times in a frame.

    Changes made here, such as impulses, take effect in the next physics
    step. Because the step length is fixed, scale any force by the time step
    and apply it as an impulse. By default this action does nothing.

    Most users never need to call this action directly.

    Attribute: Parameter timeStep The length of the physics step, in seconds.
    */
    action UpdatePhysics(number timeStep)
    end

    /*
    This action is called by a Layer3D once per frame, after all of the
    frame's physics steps have run and the items have been placed where they
    will be drawn. It is called even on frames with no physics step. Use it
    to move things that should follow the physics on screen. It should not
    change the physics itself. By default it does nothing.

    Most users never need to call this action directly.

    Attribute: Parameter seconds The time since the last frame, in seconds.
    */
    action UpdateAfterPhysics(number seconds)
    end

    /*
    This action returns how many items this behavior works with. A Layer3D
    uses this, together with GetItem, to remove the behavior when one of its
    items is removed. By default it returns 0.

    Attribute: Returns The number of items this behavior uses.
    */
    action GetItemsSize returns integer
        return 0
    end

    /*
    This action returns one of the items this behavior works with. Indexes
    start at 0 and go up to one less than GetItemsSize. By default it returns
    undefined.

    Attribute: Parameter index The index of the item to return.
    Attribute: Returns The item at that index.
    */
    action GetItem(integer index) returns Item3D
        return undefined
    end

    /*
    This action returns the layer this behavior is in, or undefined if it is
    not in a layer.

    Attribute: Returns The layer this behavior is in.
    */
    action GetLayer returns Layer3D
        return layer
    end

    /*
    This action records which layer this behavior is in. A Layer3D calls it
    when the behavior is added or removed, separately from AddedToLayer and
    RemovedFromLayer, so that GetLayer stays correct even when a subclass
    replaces those actions. Most users should never need to call this action
    directly.

    Attribute: Parameter layer The layer this behavior is in, or undefined.
    */
    action SetLayer(Layer3D layer)
        me:layer = layer
    end
end